---
import { comparison, comparisonScope } from "../../data/comparison";
import { snapshot } from "../../data/results";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Run notes and cost methodology" description="How results were produced, what the significance analysis covers, and how costs were estimated.">
  <section class="prose-lfb prose mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 pt-14 sm:px-6">
    <a href="/data/">← Data &amp; code</a>
    <h1>Run notes and cost methodology</h1>
    <h2>How runs were produced</h2>
    <p>Each configuration ran in GitHub Actions against the same locked release. Some runs needed recovery after provider or accounting issues, and some accounting fields were incomplete. The notes below explain how comparable costs were reconstructed and where estimates remain.</p>
    <h2>Result provenance</h2>
    <p>{snapshot.provenance.method}</p>
    <h2 id="summary-comparisons">Summary comparisons</h2>
    <p>The summary-pipeline comparison, including its method, provenance, costs, and significance analysis, now has its own page: <a href="/experiments/summary-pipelines/#method">Summary pipelines experiment</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="significance">Statistical comparison scope</h2>
    <p>{comparisonScope} {comparison.caveat}</p>
    <p>Untested pairs are not evidence of equivalence.</p>
    <a href="/data/#significance">Download the analysis and reproducible inputs →</a>
            <h2 id="costs">Cost methodology and explanations</h2>
            <p>Charts compare estimated standard-rate costs for the same successful 91-case workload. They do not represent total experiment spending or provider invoices. Flex discounts are removed for the chart; the successful workload charges and estimates remain available in the download.</p>
            <p>We retain cache discounts where usage and prices are known. Where cache dimensions or prices are missing, we use ordinary-input estimates. These may overstate or understate cache-adjusted costs. Failed attempts, retries, and unresolved charges are excluded.</p>
            <p><a href="/data/costs.json" download>Download cost evidence, pricing references, coverage, and run identities</a></p>
            <dl>{snapshot.models.filter(model=>model.cost.note).map(model=><div><dt>{model.display_name}</dt><dd>{model.cost.note}</dd></div>)}</dl>

  </section>
</Layout>
